From 3c4bb5c11a4502e430e78d9cab40f693783766fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:00:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): a fresh depth operation bottoms out at the part's
 floor, not the G54 plane

A new 2D Contour (and every depth kind seeded from the default Face) took
its bottom from Carried::of's fallback, WorkOffset(0)+0 - the G54 Z0
plane. With G54 Z zeroed on the part's top, a common shop habit, that
bottom resolved level with the top (TopOfModel+0), and CreateOperation
refused the zero-depth operation ("must cut downward") before the user
could open its Heights tab; the only way through was to move G54.

The fallback is now BottomOfModel+0: a fresh operation's numbers still
show where the material is (the intent of the old default), whatever
the shop's work-offset convention. fresh_depth_operations_default_to_
the_part_and_g54 pinned the old default and is updated and renamed.

Fixes #214

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
